    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12430308/comment/12730640",
          "id": "12730640",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jasonrutherglen",
            "name": "jasonrutherglen",
            "key": "jasonrutherglen",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Jason Rutherglen",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "In order for this class to be compatible with out current\ndefault LogMergePolicy, we'll need to expose readers from the IW\nreader pool. This is because presumably classes may need to\naccess readers such as in\nLogMergePolicy.findMergesToExpungeDeletes.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jasonrutherglen",
            "name": "jasonrutherglen",
            "key": "jasonrutherglen",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Jason Rutherglen",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2009-07-14T00:59:19.345+0000",
          "updated": "2009-07-14T00:59:19.345+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12430308/comment/12730644",
          "id": "12730644",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jasonrutherglen",
            "name": "jasonrutherglen",
            "key": "jasonrutherglen",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Jason Rutherglen",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "After looking at it, I wasn't sure why we couldn't simply make\nthe read only methods in SegmentInfo and SegmentInfos (and the\nclasses) public. \n\nMaybe this can make it into 2.9?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jasonrutherglen",
            "name": "jasonrutherglen",
            "key": "jasonrutherglen",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Jason Rutherglen",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2009-07-14T01:16:47.213+0000",
